# TypixDeck: Raspberry Pi OS Desktop (Trixie, arm64) for the TypixDeck
# handheld (CM5 carrier board; CM4/Zero-class modules also supported by the
# overlays), i.e. the stock stage0-4 desktop plus typixdeck-stage:
#
#   * 3.2" 1024x768 DPI panel + GT911 touch + PWM backlight overlays,
#     compiled from source and enabled in config.txt,
#   * backlight brightness tray applet in the wf-panel tray,
#   * MCU firmware + flashing tools in /opt/typixdeck/firmware,
#   * rpi-connect(-lite) and squeekboard/wfplug-squeek removed.
#
#   sudo ./build.sh -c config-typixdeck        # native arm64 host
#   ./build-docker.sh -c config-typixdeck      # in Docker
#
# NOTE on the architecture: pi-gen hardcodes ARCH per branch (master builds
# armhf, the arm64/typixdeck branches build arm64). This config lives on the
# typixdeck branch, whose build.sh targets arm64, so it works as-is; do not
# build it from a master checkout. ARCH below is declarative; the explicit
# IMG_NAME keeps the artifact name right either way.

IMG_NAME="raspios-trixie-arm64-typixdeck"
RELEASE="trixie"
ARCH="arm64"

STAGE_LIST="stage0 stage1 stage2 stage3 stage4 typixdeck-stage"

TARGET_HOSTNAME="${TARGET_HOSTNAME:-typixdeck}"

# Neutral defaults; Raspberry Pi Imager's advanced options override them all.
LOCALE_DEFAULT="${LOCALE_DEFAULT:-en_US.UTF-8}"
KEYBOARD_KEYMAP="${KEYBOARD_KEYMAP:-us}"
KEYBOARD_LAYOUT="${KEYBOARD_LAYOUT:-English (US)}"
TIMEZONE_DEFAULT="${TIMEZONE_DEFAULT:-Etc/UTC}"

# No baked-in password: the first user is customised by Raspberry Pi Imager
# (cloud-init) or the first-boot wizard, exactly like the stock images.
FIRST_USER_NAME="${FIRST_USER_NAME:-pi}"

# cloud-init is what applies Imager's customisation on Trixie; never disable
# it for a published image.
ENABLE_CLOUD_INIT="${ENABLE_CLOUD_INIT:-1}"

# Raspberry Pi Imager consumes .img.xz directly.
DEPLOY_COMPRESSION="${DEPLOY_COMPRESSION:-xz}"

# Only export the final typixdeck-stage image: stage2 (Lite) and stage4
# (Desktop) also carry EXPORT_IMAGE files, and build.sh exports every stage
# in STAGE_LIST that has one unless a SKIP_IMAGES file sits next to it.
# SKIP_IMAGES is a build-local knob (see .gitignore and README.md), so create
# the files here at build time instead of committing them - committed ones
# would break the stock Lite/Desktop builds from this same tree.
# (Remove them with `rm -f stage2/SKIP_IMAGES stage4/SKIP_IMAGES` before
# building a stock image from this checkout again.)
touch "${BASE_DIR}/stage2/SKIP_IMAGES" "${BASE_DIR}/stage4/SKIP_IMAGES"
